 "note": "    uv run python tools/e1v2_clustered.py A reanalysis of the stored scores; no model is called and no stored file is changed. The frozen scorer gives 95% Wilson intervals over case-repeats, which treat the two repeats of a case as independent. Here each case is a cluster (both repeats, and every arm of a case-repeat, stay together):   intervals    Wilson intervals on the effective sample size n / deff, where the design                effect deff is the cluster-robust variance of the rate divided by its binomial                variance, bounded below by 1 and above by the largest cluster (2). A rate of 0                or 1 has no estimable deff and takes the bound 2, i.e. one unit per case.                A case bootstrap (percentile, 10,000 draws) is stored beside it for comparison.   differences  paired differences between arms over the same case-repeats, in percentage                points, with a case bootstrap interval and the number of discordant case-repeats.   failures     each change-notice case-repeat put in exactly one class, in this order: model                abstention, contract rejection, error cycle, no change committed, wrong plant,                wrong weeks, value outside the stated interval, covered.   categories   abstentions, coverage and violations per category and model.",
